  "knowledge": "H-1B Dependency Status",
  "description": "Illustrates what it means for an employer to be H-1B dependent.",
  "definition": "An employer is considered H-1B dependent when the proportion of H-1B workers relative to the total workforce exceeds specific thresholds: 15% for employers with more than 50 employees, 8 workers for employers with 26-50 employees, or 4 workers for employers with 25 or fewer employees. H-1B dependent employers face additional attestation requirements. This status is tracked as part of the application data."
}

{
